Response:
"Broken access control happens when applications don't properly verify if a user should
access a resource. I'll use an e-commerce example:

VULNERABILITY:
An order endpoint /orders/12345 checks if user is logged in, but doesn't verify
they own that order. An attacker can change URLs to /orders/12344, /orders/12346,
