ROOT CAUSE:
Frontend only checks authentication (who are you?), but backend doesn't check
authorization (can you access this?).

SOLUTION:
Every endpoint must verify:
1. Is user authenticated? (logged in)
2. Does user own this resource? (user_id matches)
3. Does user have permission? (role allows action)

The fix is adding a check:
if order.user_id != current_user.id:
    return 403 Forbidden

Additionally, we should:
- Use consistent authorization library across all endpoints
- Fail securely (deny by default)
- Log all authorization failures
- Test every endpoint with different user roles
"
